{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>To the priest who offers it.</b> You might say to him alone; therefore Scripture says, <b>to all the sons of Aaron it shall belong</b>. You might say to all of them; therefore Scripture says, <b>to the priest who offers it</b>. How so? To the father's house of the day — those who offer it, that is to say, the men of the watch. For the priests were divided into twenty-four watches and would rotate every single Sabbath, as Jehoiada said (II Chronicles 23:8): those who come on the Sabbath with those who go out on the Sabbath. And whatever offerings came their way each and every Sabbath they would divide equally among themselves, as Scripture says (Deuteronomy 18:8): ״חלק כחלק יאכלו״ — they shall eat a portion like the portion. And Scripture mentioned all the meal-offerings by their names — baked in the oven, in the pan, and on the griddle — and afterwards returned and generalized, saying 'each man like his brother,' so that this one should have only what that one has; and even the meal-offering of fine flour they shall divide. And Scripture stated this ruling regarding meal-offerings, and all the more so regarding the rest of the offerings, whose value is greater, for it is fitting that they divide them equally — because the reward of offering belongs to the pure priests found there, since all of them offer either by hand or by command: whether the individual among them, or the two or three who officiate as emissaries, all of them act and all of them stand over the offering as emissaries — (I Samuel 30:24) ״כחלק היורד במלחמה וכחלק היושב על הכלים יחדיו יחלוקו״ — as the share of the one who goes down to battle, so the share of the one who stays by the baggage; together they shall divide. This is the language of the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:44.289635179Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}